# Skills catalog

This directory is the **source of truth** for skills. Edit `SKILL.md` here; never edit the
generated adapters under `.claude/skills/` or `.github/instructions/`. After any change,
run `{% if task_runner == "just" %}just sync-adapters{% else %}node tools/sync-adapters.mjs{% endif %}`.

A skill is a directory with a `SKILL.md` (YAML frontmatter `name` + `description`, then a
Markdown body) and optional `references/` loaded on demand. The `description` is the
**trigger** — it decides when the skill loads.

## Workflow skills (stack-agnostic, shipped)

| Skill | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `plan` | A focused, single-PR change — grills, then branch → execute → verify → PR. |
| `grill-me` | Stress-testing a plan or design before writing code. |
| `decision-making` | A choice the user should own — ask, don't assume. |
| `execute-tasks` | Several independent task files → parallel subagents, one PR. |
| `create-skill` | Authoring a new **domain** skill for your stack. |
{% if include_sdd -%}
| `sdd-spec` → `sdd-plan` → `sdd-tasks` → `sdd-implement` | The SDD pipeline (see `docs/sdd-workflow.md`). |
| `sdd-review` / `sdd-fix-review` | Review round and remediation. |
| `sdd-verify` | The fresh-evidence gate before any "done". |
| `sdd-memory` | Durable, feature-scoped context across sessions. |
{% endif -%}
{% if include_pr_review_ai -%}
| `pr-review` | Multi-dimension review of a pull request. |
{% endif %}

## Domain skills (yours, generated with `create-skill`)

Stack-specific guardrails live here too, once you author them. They trigger by path and
should also be listed in the `AGENTS.md` domain table. None ship by default — the harness
stays portable.

